  "id": "DrugBank_DB05013 - MONDO_8420",
  "verbalization": "Ingenol Mebutate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Seborrheic Keratosis through a multi-step mechanism involving the induction of cellular proliferation and differentiation. The evidence suggests that Ingenol Mebutate may act as a mediator in the progression of Seborrheic Keratosis by influencing the pathways associated with Actinic Cheilitis and Aminolevulinic Acid. These pathways are linked to the development of Seborrheic Keratosis through the activation of cellular processes that promote abnormal keratinization and proliferation. The presence of a direct indication from Ingenol Mebutate to Seborrheic Keratosis in multiple paths underscores the potential for a mechanistic link, particularly through the involvement of pathways that may be dysregulated in the condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Ingenol Mebutate could exert its effects by modulating cellular processes that contribute to the development of Seborrheic Keratosis, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the exact mechanism.",
